{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130475-wingardium-leviosah-cuiva-nwalca-carnirass\u00eb-fuego-fthagn-magic-words-usage","id":1130475,"title":"Wingardium LeviosAH, Cuiva nwalca Carnirass\u00eb!, Fuego, Fthagn - magic words usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T14:18:37-07:00","id":1130475,"title":"Wingardium LeviosAH, Cuiva nwalca Carnirass\u00eb!, Fuego, Fthagn - magic words usage","content":"So, this is probably completely unneeded, but since it came up in one of my games by accident and helped me flesh out my char. Now, I have actually made a short list with Cthuvian/R'lyehian phrases for certain spells (and all my rotes). I think, consistency like that adds something to the character/experience, and having rooted this in a language that just sounds/looks fantastic makes things even more fun.<br /> <br /> What phrases and magical formulae do you use when you do not resort to High Speech, or how do you fluff the sound of High Speech?<br /> Do you even act out the speaking of spells when they are chanted?<br /> <br /> (The above examples are, of course, Harry Potter, Lord of the Rings, Dresden Files, Call of Cthulhu. Any other systems that could be used like this? Earthsea apparently only ever identified Tolk (stone), which is a bit meagre.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I cannot believe I've blundered like this, and completely neglected Dovah-Zul, the Dragon language from Skyrim. Ah well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-17-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:29:42-07:00","id":1130482,"title":"","content":"Because of the art in first edition, and Pathfinder being fun, I tend to run High Speech as creating floating runes one can generally see if you're a mage. I've got no idea how it sounds, so it's all just 'the words for this and that.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:54:33-07:00","id":1130509,"title":"","content":"An example of High Speech visuals I used so my players would get it immediately was the Word Walls from Skyrim, expect only Mages can spot them. That, plus some imagery from comics and other movies. Neil Gaiman, Warren Ellis, Alan Moore and Garth Morrison help. I often pick up the books and show them to people, when I want to explain Mage's visuals<br /> <br /> Speaking wise, I use words from the Cthulhu Mythos as well because I'm me. I also use some terminology from Stephen King's books, especially the Dark Tower. <i>Ka, </i>and such. Not much well known, but it does its job","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-17-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:03:30-07:00","id":1130520,"title":"","content":"I like Ideograms and logograms for High Speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:10:28-07:00","id":1130566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130475-wingardium-leviosah-cuiva-nwalca-carnirass\u00eb-fuego-fthagn-magic-words-usage?p=1130520#post1130520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Ideograms and logograms for High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with those, will have to google-check, thanks!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> nice! Haven't thought about the Dark Tower. Hm.<br /> Regarding Chtulhu Mythos, it is nice that some people went through the work to make the language into a semi-cohesive system that can be sort-of used =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}